"Official Build" means a build of the Software that the Licensor distributes,
for example through the App Store, Google Play or the Licensor's own website,
together with everything such a build installs, builds or runs on your devices
and servers as part of its normal operation.

"Contribution" means a change to the Software that you send to the Licensor
for review under CONTRIBUTING.md.

2. What you may do without a license

(a) Read and view the Software. Apart from (b), copying it, including
    forking it on GitHub, is not allowed by this license.
(b) Download the Software to read it, to review its security, or to report a
    problem to the Licensor.
(c) Change the Software only to send the change to the Licensor for review,
    and send it to the Licensor. Such a change may not be compiled, run,
    kept, published or shared for any other purpose, and the Licensor may
    reject it without reason. Problems and ideas may also be sent in words.
(d) Quote short excerpts for commentary, review or discussion, with
    attribution.

3. What needs a commercial license

Everything not allowed by section 2 is forbidden unless the Licensor agrees in
